INT. ST. BRIDGET'S CHURCH BASEMENT - NIGHT

Fluorescent tubes. HUMMING. A coffee urn GURGLES.

Folding chairs in a circle. Eight empty. One taken.

TESS HALLORAN, 17, slumps in it. Backpack on her knees. Court-ordered slip crushed in her fist.

Rain. Hammering the high windows.

The DOOR BANGS open.

A WOMAN storms in. Fifties. Soaked. Leather jacket. Keys in a white-knuckle grip.

She stops. Stares at Tess.

THE WOMAN
You're in my chair.

TESS
There's no name on it.

Silence.

The Woman drops into the next seat. The chair SCREECHES.

THE WOMAN (CONT'D)
You're a kid.

TESS
Seventeen.

THE WOMAN
Seventeen. Great.

Tess pulls out her phone. Taps. Taps again.

Her phone. Dead.

TESS
Nobody else is coming?

THE WOMAN
Flooded out on Delancey. It's us.

The urn CLICKS off. Quiet.

Tess stands. Grabs her bag.

TESS
Then I'm out. She said I only needed a signature.

THE WOMAN
She who?

TESS
The judge.

THE WOMAN
She signs nothing unless you sit.

Tess freezes. Thunder. A long ROLL.

Nothing.

The Woman leans forward. Elbows on knees. She meets Tess's eyes.

THE WOMAN (CONT'D)
Eleven years sober. Tuesday. Her birthday. My daughter's.

TESS
Why are you telling me that?

THE WOMAN
Because she wouldn't open the door either.

Tess's jaw tightens.

TESS
That's not fair.

The Woman holds out a hand.

THE WOMAN
Greta.

Tess stares at it. A beat.

Lightning. The lights FLICKER.

Tess shakes it.

TESS
Tess.

GRETA
Sit, Tess.

Tess sits.

Rain.

GRETA (CONT'D)
You go first.

TESS
(barely audible)
Hi. I'm Tess.

GRETA
Hi, Tess.

The lights HOLD.
